  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, concat; acc≈0.435), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal setup is actually outperforming a unimodal baseline. config_043 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) changes only the model setting relative to config_001 while keeping the same image encoder and profile setting, cleanly isolating the contribution of the RNA modality. If image-only performs comparably to 0.435, the RNA branch or fusion is not adding value and subsequent experiments should target representation or fusion improvements; if it is substantially lower, multimodal fusion is confirmed as beneficial and we can exploit that direction. Establishing this baseline before varying encoders, aggregation, or fusion is the highest-information single experiment under a tight budget, since it determines whether the entire multimodal search space is worth exploring further."
}

